@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: retire the workspace .env as a credential path in favour of keys the host store holds once — and the four things that block it
' PLANNED — nothing here is implemented; _spec/_plans/ is exempt from the SPEC-reference rule.
'   where a key rests between runs  _spec/_plans/secret-custody.puml
'   the file this would replace ..... _spec/_plans/workspace-env-key.puml
'   who injects on sbx today ....... _spec/internal/sbx/credential-path.puml
'   what the agent may hold ........ _spec/_paradigms/credential-boundary.puml
'   the gate that decides a service  _spec/internal/sbx/kit-sandbox-credential-gap.puml
'   the store's own hazard, realised _spec/internal/sbx/kit-sandbox-credential-gap.puml
'   the code .... internal/backend/sandbox/sandbox.go (agentCredentials, Spec)
'   the code .... internal/sbx/secret.go (SecretSetArgs), internal/sbx/run.go (StoredSecretNames)
'   the code .... packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh (load_env), internal/entrypoint/entrypoint.go (ShouldSkipEnvLoad)
'
' ── THE PROPOSAL, IN THE OPERATOR'S WORDS ──────────────────────────────────
' "sbx sets credentials once on the host. Having keys in the .env file is
' unsafe, a better bet would be prompting sbx to input keys."
'
' It is the right direction and half of it already works. What follows is the
' half that does not, measured rather than predicted, because every blocker
' below was hit for real in the session that produced this plan.
'
' ── WHAT IS ALREADY TRUE (measured 2026-09-09, live sandbox) ───────────────
'   the agent holds SENTINELS ONLY. /proc/<pid>/environ of the cecli process
'     carries XAI_API_KEY=proxy-managed and six more. No real key is in the
'     agent, which is the whole property credential-boundary.puml asks for.
'   the proxy REPLACES the header. `Authorization: Bearer xai-junk` sent from
'     inside the sandbox came back with the stored account's own error, so the
'     substitution is real and not merely declared.
'   a stored API-key secret injects a WORKING value. sbx-kit-capabilities.puml
'     lists that as unproven; for an api-key service it is now proven. An
'     OAuth-backed service is still untested.
' So the mechanism the proposal wants is shipped. The gap is custody, not
' capability.
'
' ── BLOCKER 1: THE STORE IS WRITE-ONLY, GLOBAL, AND NEVER EXPIRES ──────────
' This is the one that cost a whole session, so it goes first.
'
' `sbx secret ls` prints scope and name and NOT value — there is no `get`. The
' store is `(global)`: shared by every sandbox on the host, outliving every run,
' with no expiry and no rotation. credential-path.puml already wrote down the
' consequence — "a stale entry from an earlier run can therefore authenticate a
' later one that never chose it" — and then it happened:
'
'   an old credprobe experiment had left a secret under the service name `xai`
'   proveo pushed the operator's CURRENT key under `XAI_API_KEY`, which nothing
'     reads on the sandbox-kind path
'   so the proxy injected the EXPERIMENT's key, whose team was out of credits
'   xAI answered 403, the agent rendered "403 Client Error", and the operator
'     read an egress denial
'
' Identifying the loaded key needed a round trip to the PROVIDER:
' `GET api.x.ai/v1/api-key` echoes name, id, redacted suffix and team. That
' works because xAI describes its own credential; most vendors do not, so it is
' a trick and not a mechanism.
'
' CENTRALISING MORE KEYS INTO AN OPAQUE STORE MAKES THIS WORSE, NOT BETTER. The
' proposal is only safe once an operator can answer "which key authenticates
' this run" without asking the vendor. That is the first thing to build.
'
' ── BLOCKER 2: THE TWO NAMES STILL DO NOT MEET ─────────────────────────────
'   `sbx secret set xai`         what the proxy resolves (kit reference: the
'                                service field is "matched against the value
'                                stored with sbx secret set", kebab-case)
'   `sbx secret set XAI_API_KEY` what proveo writes, every run, from the host
'                                environment — and what nothing consumes here
'
' proveo cannot simply write the service name: TestSpecNeverStoresAService-
' NamedSecret forbids it, and its message records why — it was measured
' overwriting an operator's OAuth login. So "prompt once" means prompting for
' SERVICE names, and proveo's env-var entries become noise in the same listing.
' Either proveo stops writing them on this path, or it explains both.
'
' ── BLOCKER 3: CONSENT IS INTERACTIVE, ONCE PER SERVICE ────────────────────
' sbx asks for consent the first time a service is injected, records it in
' ~/.config/sbx/credentials.yaml, and asks even for a credential it already
' holds — the screen reads "(stored)" and still prompts
' (sbx-kit-capabilities.puml). An unattended run stops there. So a host has to
' be PRIMED before it can be automated, which is the opposite of "set it once
' and forget it" unless priming is an explicit, visible step.
'
' ── BLOCKER 4: NOT EVERY PROVIDER CAN BE INJECTED AT ALL ───────────────────
' `agentCredentials` skips a provider when there is nothing to attach:
'   signed requests   bedrock, azure, vertex — SigV4 and friends sign the whole
'                     request, so no header carries the secret
'   query parameter   sbx injects into a header and has no query form;
'                     declaring one would sentinel the variable and attach the
'                     value nowhere, which is strictly worse than leaving it
' Those providers still need a real value in the environment. So `.env` SHRINKS
' rather than disappears, and any plan that says "retired" is overclaiming.
'
' ── THE SMALLEST FIRST STEP, AND IT IS NOT A NEW MECHANISM ─────────────────
' `load_env` already refuses to source a dotenv when PROVEO_EGRESS_MODE names a
' canonical tier — it prints "🔒 Skipping .env load … secrets stay on host /
' broker". The sbx Kit sets no such variable, so the branch never fires. The
' Kit already carries an `environment.variables` map (MCP_GATEWAY_URL lives
' there), so this is one entry.
'
' It is worth doing even though clone mode already keeps a gitignored `.env` out
' of the sandbox, because clone mode is a DEFAULT and not a guarantee:
' `--clone=false`, a sub-scope, a non-repo, a linked worktree and a COMMITTED
' `.env` all fall back to the mounted tree.
'
' Spell the flag honestly. The tier vocabulary is deliberately inert on sbx
' (policy-baseline.puml), so `PROVEO_EGRESS_MODE=allowlist` there would smuggle
' a meaningless value; a purpose-named flag belongs in
' internal/contract/egress_vocabulary_test.go alongside the tiers.
'
' ── WHAT THIS PLAN DELIBERATELY DOES NOT DECIDE ────────────────────────────
' WHERE THE BYTES REST. Whether sbx keeps secret values in the macOS Keychain
' or in a sandboxd-owned file is unmeasured — the `sbx secret` docs page
' rendered empty — and it changes the threat model completely. secret-custody
' .puml owns that question; this plan owns the custody WORKFLOW.
'
' WHETHER A COMMITTED .env SHOULD REFUSE A RUN. Named in workspace-env-key.puml
' and still open there.
'
' WHETHER `load_env` SHOULD SOURCE DOTENVS AT ALL now that a broker and a host
' store both exist. Removing it outright would break the docker firewall tier
' and every non-injectable provider from Blocker 4.
title PLANNED — provider keys held once on the host, and the four things\nbetween that and retiring the workspace .env

component "**""<ws>/.env""**\na key at rest beside the code" as ENVF <<error>>
node "the host" as HOST <<host>> {
  database "sbx secret store\n""(global)"" · no ""get"" · no expiry" as STORE <<db>>
  component "proveo\nwrites ""XAI_API_KEY"" — unread here" as PV <<error>>
  component "the operator\nprompted once, per SERVICE" as OP <<app>>
}
cloud "sbx proxy\nreplaces the header" as PROXY <<cloud>>
component "the agent\nsentinels only — measured" as AGENT <<app>>
component "signed + query providers\nbedrock · azure · vertex" as UNINJ <<error>>
component "**the stale key**\nauthenticated a run nobody chose" as STALE <<error>>

OP ARROW_MAIN STORE : ""sbx secret set xai""
PV ARROW_ERROR STORE : ""XAI_API_KEY"" — a name\nnothing resolves
STORE ARROW_QUEUE PROXY : resolved by SERVICE name
PROXY ARROW_MAIN AGENT : header attached at egress
STORE ARROW_ERROR STALE : an entry outlives every run
ENVF ARROW_ERROR AGENT : the path to close
UNINJ ARROW_ERROR ENVF : these cannot be injected,\nso the file survives for them

note bottom of STORE
  **Write-only, global, permanent.** ""ls"" shows
  names, never values; the scope is the whole
  host; nothing expires. Centralising keys into
  it is only safe once an operator can see which
  one authenticates a run.
end note

note bottom of STALE
  **It already happened.** An old credprobe left
  ""xai"" behind; the proxy injected it; its team
  was out of credits; the agent printed a 403 and
  it read as an egress block.
end note

note bottom of PV
  **proveo writes the wrong name, on purpose.**
  The service name is refused because it was
  measured clobbering an OAuth login — so
  ""prompt once"" means prompting for services,
  and the env-var entries become noise.
end note

note right of AGENT
  **This half is done.** ""/proc/<pid>/environ""
  shows sentinels only, and a junk bearer sent
  from inside still reached the stored account.
  The gap is custody, not capability.
end note

note bottom of UNINJ
  **Signed requests have no header to hold.**
  SigV4 signs the whole request, and sbx has no
  query-param form, so these keep needing a real
  value in the environment. The file shrinks; it
  does not vanish.
end note

legend bottom
  **The order to do it in**
  ==
  **1. Stop the file being sourced on sbx.** ""load_env"" already skips when a flag
  says so; the Kit sets no flag, and it already has an ""environment.variables"" map.
  One entry, purpose-named — not the tier vocabulary, which is inert on that backend.
  --
  **2. Make the store legible before putting more in it.** An operator must be able
  to ask "which key authenticates this service" without a round trip to the vendor.
  A stale entry answering for a run nobody chose is the failure this plan exists for.
  ==
  **3. Reconcile the two names.** proveo writes ""<VAR>_API_KEY"", sbx resolves the
  service name, and both sit in one listing. Either stop writing the unread one on
  this path, or show the operator which of the pair is live.
  --
  **4. Make priming an explicit step.** First injection per service prompts, even for
  a stored credential, so an unattended host must be primed deliberately rather than
  by accident — which is how the stale ""xai"" got there in the first place.
  ==
  **Not decided here**: where sbx keeps the bytes (Keychain or a daemon file — unmeasured,
  and it changes the threat model); whether a committed "".env"" should refuse a run; whether
  ""load_env"" should source dotenvs at all, given the docker firewall tier and Blocker 4.
end legend
@enduml
